From: radeon-custom rs480 reset-recovery track
Subject: [PATCH] drm/radeon: advance fbdev write ppos when GPU is parked

When the GPU is parked, radeon_fbdev_fb_write returns success without
touching VRAM so fbcon cannot hang the host. VFS still advances the file
position from *ppos on a short/success write path, so leaving *ppos
unchanged makes the next write retry the same offset forever.

Advance *ppos by the swallowed count on the parked success path so the
caller observes a normal write completion.

--- a/radeon/radeon_fbdev.c
+++ b/radeon/radeon_fbdev.c
@@ -204,8 +204,14 @@
 				     const char __user *buf, size_t count,
 				     loff_t *ppos)
 {
-	if (radeon_fbdev_gpu_parked(info))
+	if (radeon_fbdev_gpu_parked(info)) {
+		/* VFS advances file position from *ppos; a success return
+		 * without advancing it makes the next write retry the same
+		 * offset forever. Advance as if the swallowed write landed.
+		 */
+		*ppos += count;
 		return count;
+	}
 	return fb_io_write(info, buf, count, ppos);
 }
 
